I can't make a pull request right now, so I'll just comment.

This is OpenCV bug. 

https://github.com/opencv/opencv/blob/315f85d4f484c1e2fa043c73ac3fdd9fc5997ee7/modules/imgproc/src/cornersubpix.cpp#L95-L101

`Rect(0, 0, src.cols, src.rows)` has integer type. ( `typedef Rect2i cv::Rect` )
`cT` has float32 type,
`cT` will be rounding to integer and comparing with `Rect(...)`. 
So it is failed.

The following patch has been confirmed to be effective.
(I'm sorry I didn't test for side-effects )

```diff
diff --git a/modules/imgproc/src/cornersubpix.cpp b/modules/imgproc/src/cornersubpix.cpp
index af5bd999dc..431fd6eecb 100644
--- a/modules/imgproc/src/cornersubpix.cpp
+++ b/modules/imgproc/src/cornersubpix.cpp
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@ void cv::cornerSubPix( InputArray _image, InputOutputArray _corners,
     for( int pt_i = 0; pt_i < count; pt_i++ )
     {
         Point2f cT = corners[pt_i], cI = cT;
-        CV_Assert( Rect(0, 0, src.cols, src.rows).contains(cT) );
+        CV_Assert( Rect2f(0, 0, src.cols, src.rows).contains(cT) );
         int iter = 0;
         double err = 0;
```
